Z||000003||batboy||03-19-2000||06:22 AM||||Yes...he has taken that final step to Fiero manhood. Welcome brother!<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 03-19-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||03-19-2000||03:40 PM||||Advatages of the 4 puck.. VERY positive engagement, ablility to chirp the tires in any gear anytime you like and at ANY speed; the real reason it was put in..  It will hold the 200+ foot pounds of torque we are adding with the nitrous. Mine chatters a bit.. as does Todds but it's a small price to pay for not having to worry about anything slipping and cooking a stock clutch and having to replace another one in 2 weeks been there.. done that... Disadvantages, Shakes the dash a bit on engagment(chatter), tires spin really easy in the rain, more shock to the tranny, cost. but mine seems fine.. has 6 months worth the BEATING on it and shes still fine... The Pressure plate he is using is a modified Borg & Beck (basicly stock with a heavyier clamping force) That was $75. the 4 Puck dics itself retails for $130. and the throw out bearing is/was $20 so for $225 you'll have the parts needed for a high torque motor. My Pressure plate was $140 has a clamping force of 1500# (ACT extreme, Advanced Clutch Technology) about 55% more than stock. not sure of their web site.. i'll go find it. you can see their products and specs in Turbo and High tech magazine <A HREF="http://www.turbomagazine.com" TARGET=_blank>www.turbomagazine.com</A>  and Sport compact Car.. not sure of thier site... ||||reg||1
Z||000005||BlackGT||03-20-2000||10:10 AM||||Well folks as 1fst2m6 has stated I became an<BR>ameture fiero mechanic, and after some very colorful words, quite a few hours of labor,<BR>donating some blood sweat and tears to the <BR>effort "Misty" is back on the road! Yes I`m afraid I have been out mooostang hunting but<BR>no success as of yet. I have however surprised a BMW M5 owner. After I showed him<BR>my plate for a while he boldly asked when did<BR>Pontiac start making rockets! I replied back <BR>in the 80`s before the accountants took over!<BR>Yes the dash shakes when I try to slip this<BR>clutch in heavy traffic on 285 in Atlanta but<BR>overall I like it. The pressure plate allows<BR>for a lite feel on the pedal but when you let<BR>off the transaxle is locked....NO MORE SLIPPING! We looked at my flywheel and realized what was going on.....the mechanic<BR>that put in my stock clutch didn`t resurface<BR>the flywheel! My old clutch disc is fine but<BR>since I had this baby open the 4puck went in<BR>anyway...after all that trouble. I`ve never<BR>done anything like this in my life and I can <BR>honestly say I won`t do it again....I don`t like being without my baby too long nor see her ass up in the air on stands! I took pics<BR>to remind me not to do this job without a lift......it sooo much easier to stand and wrench than laying on your back underneath<BR>this go cart. Well next up is the dyno session then onto the throttle body bypass then the "BLUE BOTTLE".............||||reg||6
